From 0bfb5ff1bd0aa004919443422a8df6caab1778df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:13:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Base the edge array before the element-count check in
 `dmeshLoadAdm()` [report R. Perry]

On the `bad input (2)` path, `dmeshLoadAdm()` did `goto fail` before
`eelmloctax` was rebased, yet the fail block frees `eelmloctax + baseval`;
for a non-zero base this would free a pointer inside the block. The
branch is currently unreachable (the earlier header-consistency check
forces the element-count sum to match), so this is latent, but the free
of an unbased pointer is fragile.

Rebase the edge array right after the distribution array is built, before
the element-count check, so both the check's fail path and the normal
path free the based pointer. All arrays are known to be allocated at that
point (a prior allocation failure returns earlier).

Refs: DGR-16
---
 src/libscotch/dmesh_io_load.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/dmesh_io_load.c b/src/libscotch/dmesh_io_load.c
index d501be1..6630c5d 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/dmesh_io_load.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/dmesh_io_load.c
@@ -315,15 +315,17 @@ const DmeshFlag             flagval)              /* Mesh loading flags
     preldspadj += preldspval;
   }
   prelvrttab[procnum] = preldspadj;               /* Set end of displacement array */
-  if (preldspadj != (velmglbnbr + baseval)) {
+
+  vnodglbnnd  = vnodglbnbr + baseval;
+  eelmloctax -= baseval;                          /* Base edge array with new base (all arrays allocated by now) */
+  eelmlocnnd  = eelmlocnbr + baseval;
+
+  if (preldspadj != (velmglbnbr + baseval)) {     /* After basing, so that the fail path frees the based array */
     errorPrint ("dmeshLoadAdm: bad input (2)");
     reduloctab[0] = 1;
     goto fail;
   }
 
-  vnodglbnnd  = vnodglbnbr + baseval;
-  eelmloctax -= baseval;                          /* Base edge array with new base */
-  eelmlocnnd  = eelmlocnbr + baseval;
   for (velmlocnum = 0, eelmlocnum = baseval; velmlocnum < velmlocnbr; velmlocnum ++) {
     Gnum                degrval;                  /* Number of neighbors for element */
 
